## 3. Checkpoint Saver Bean (durable state)

```java
@Configuration
@EnableConfigurationProperties(AgentProperties.class)
public class CheckpointConfiguration {

    @Bean(destroyMethod = "close")
    public PostgresSaver checkpointSaver(AgentProperties props) throws Exception {
        var cp = props.checkpoint();
        return PostgresSaver.builder()
                .host(cp.host())
                .port(cp.port())
                .database(cp.database())
                .user(cp.user())
                .password(cp.password())
                .stateSerializer(new ObjectStreamStateSerializer<>(AgentExecutor.State::new))
                .createTables(true)   // idempotent; use migrations in strict envs
                .build();
    }
}
```

> This is what makes the app **production-grade**: every graph step is checkpointed to Postgres. If a pod dies mid-conversation, the thread resumes exactly where it stopped, and conversation memory survives restarts and scales across replicas.

## 4. Tools — real business logic, injectable, testable

```java
@Component
public class OrderTools {

    private static final Logger log = LoggerFactory.getLogger(OrderTools.class);

    private final OrderRepository orders;
    private final RefundService refunds;

    public OrderTools(OrderRepository orders, RefundService refunds) {
        this.orders = orders;
        this.refunds = refunds;
    }

    @Tool(description = "Look up an order by its ID. Returns status, items and total.")
    public String getOrder(
            @ToolParam(description = "The order ID, e.g. ORD-12345") String orderId) {
        log.info("tool:getOrder orderId={}", orderId);
        return orders.findById(orderId)
                .map(o -> "Order %s | status=%s | total=%s | items=%s"
                        .formatted(o.id(), o.status(), o.total(), o.itemSummary()))
                .orElse("No order found with ID " + orderId);
    }

    @Tool(description = "Request a refund for a delivered order. Returns a ticket ID.")
    public String requestRefund(
            @ToolParam(description = "The order ID") String orderId,
            @ToolParam(description = "Reason given by the customer") String reason) {
        log.info("tool:requestRefund orderId={} reason={}", orderId, reason);
        try {
            return "Refund ticket created: " + refunds.open(orderId, reason).ticketId();
        } catch (RefundNotAllowedException e) {
            // Return the failure AS TEXT so the LLM can explain it to the user
            return "Refund rejected: " + e.getMessage();
        }
    }
}
```

**Key production rule:** tools should *return* error descriptions instead of throwing, so the LLM can recover gracefully instead of crashing the graph.

## 5. The Agent Service — graph built once, invoked per request

```java
@Service
public class SupportAgentService {

    private static final Logger log = LoggerFactory.getLogger(SupportAgentService.class);

    private final CompiledGraph<AgentExecutor.State> graph;

    public SupportAgentService(ChatModel chatModel,
                               OrderTools orderTools,
                               PostgresSaver checkpointSaver,
                               AgentProperties props) throws GraphStateException {

        var stateGraph = AgentExecutor.builder()
                .chatModel(chatModel)
                .toolsFromObject(orderTools)
                .defaultSystem(props.systemPrompt())
                .build();

        this.graph = stateGraph.compile(CompileConfig.builder()
                .checkpointSaver(checkpointSaver)
                .releaseThread(false)          // keep thread state -> conversation memory
                .build());
    }

    /**
     * One conversation turn. threadId isolates state per user+conversation,
     * so the agent remembers previous turns automatically via checkpoints.
     */
    public String chat(String userId, String conversationId, String userMessage) {
        var config = RunnableConfig.builder()
                .threadId(userId + ":" + conversationId)
                .putMetadata("userId", userId)
                .build();

        try {
            var result = graph.stream(Map.of("messages", new UserMessage(userMessage)), config)
                    .stream()
                    .peek(step -> log.debug("node executed: {}", step.node()))
                    .reduce((a, b) -> b)
                    .orElseThrow(() -> new AgentException("Graph produced no output"));

            return result.state().lastMessage()
                    .filter(AssistantMessage.class::isInstance)
                    .map(AssistantMessage.class::cast)
                    .map(AssistantMessage::getText)
                    .orElseThrow(() -> new AgentException("No assistant response in final state"));

        } catch (Exception e) {
            log.error("Agent execution failed for thread {}", conversationId, e);
            throw new AgentException("Agent failed to process the request", e);
        }
    }

    /** Audit / debugging: full checkpoint history of a conversation. */
    public Collection<StateSnapshot<AgentExecutor.State>> history(String userId, String conversationId) {
        return graph.getStateHistory(RunnableConfig.builder()
                .threadId(userId + ":" + conversationId)
                .build());
    }
}
```

## 6. REST Controller with validation & error handling

```java
@RestController
@RequestMapping("/api/chat")
public class ChatController {

    private final SupportAgentService agent;

    public ChatController(SupportAgentService agent) {
        this.agent = agent;
    }

    public record ChatRequest(
            @NotBlank @Size(max = 4000) String message,
            @NotBlank String conversationId) {}

    public record ChatResponse(String reply, String conversationId) {}

    @PostMapping
    public ChatResponse chat(@AuthenticationPrincipal Jwt jwt,   // or your auth mechanism
                             @Valid @RequestBody ChatRequest req) {
        String reply = agent.chat(jwt.getSubject(), req.conversationId(), req.message());
        return new ChatResponse(reply, req.conversationId());
    }
}

@RestControllerAdvice
class AgentExceptionHandler {

    @ExceptionHandler(AgentException.class)
    ResponseEntity<Map<String, String>> handle(AgentException e) {
        return ResponseEntity.status(HttpStatus.SERVICE_UNAVAILABLE)
                .body(Map.of("error", "The assistant is temporarily unavailable. Please retry."));
    }
}
```

